<h1>
  番茄果實整合蛋白質體／轉錄組分析(Integrated Proteome/Transcriptome Profiling of Tomato Fruit)
</h1>

<div class="indentedcontent">

  <div style="width: 330px; float: right" class="captioned_image img_float_right">

    <img src="/img/secretom/tomato_array_300.jpg" />

  </div>

  <p>
  我們正在將<a href="http://ted.bti.cornell.edu">番茄果實轉錄表現分析計畫(tomato fruit transcript expression profiling initiative)</a>與細胞壁蛋白質體分析相結合，涵蓋野生型成熟果實以及成熟受損突變體（ripening inhibitor [rin]、non-ripening [Nor] 和 never ripe [Nr]）。轉錄組數據是使用 8,700 個單基因 TOM1 cDNA 晶片、長寡核苷酸 12,000 單基因 (TOM2) 微陣列晶片以及兩個 RNASeq 平台（454 和 Illumina）產生的。(We are integrating a <a href="http://ted.bti.cornell.edu">tomato fruit transcript expression profiling initiative</a> with the cell wall proteome analysis, in both wild type ripening fruit and those of the ripening impaired mutants ripening inhibitor (rin), non-ripening (Nor) and never ripe (Nr). The transcriptome data is being generated with the 8,700 unigene TOM1 cDNA array, the long oligonucleotide 12,000 unigene (TOM2) microarrays and two RNASeq platforms (454 and Illumina).)
  </p>

  <p>
  透過將質譜衍生的蛋白質序列分析與番茄微陣列的互補序列進行比對，識別基因及其同源蛋白質後，直接比對該基因集的微陣列和蛋白質體數據，以識別：(a) 透過果實發育或與突變果實相比，蛋白質體分析顯示顯著表現變化但微陣列分析未顯示變化（或反之亦然）的基因；(b) 轉錄本與同源蛋白水平變化之間存在顯著差異的基因。(Following the identification of genes and their cognate proteins through comparison of MS-derived protein sequence analysis with the complement of the tomato microarray, microarray and proteomics data of this gene set are directly compared to identify: (a) genes showing significant expression changes by proteomic analysis but not by microarray analysis, or vice versa, through fruit development, or in comparison with mutant fruits; (b) genes showing significant differences between changes in transcript and cognate protein levels.)
  </p>
</div>

<&| /secretom/section_templates/objectives.mas, is_subsection => 1 &>

  使用相關性分析比對上述各組中每個基因的蛋白質和轉錄組譜，並定義三個不同類別：在微陣列和蛋白質體分析之間顯示正相關、負相關或無顯著相關者。(Compare the protein and transcriptome profile of each gene in the groups above using correlation analysis and define three different categories: those showing positive, negative or no significant correlation between microarray and proteomic analysis.)

  如果產生足夠大小的數據集，各組中代表的基因數量將用於估算受轉錄和／或轉錄後調控的分泌組基因。(If data sets of sufficient size result, the number of genes represented in each group will be used to derive estimates of secretome genes under transcriptional and/or post-transcriptional control.)

  將基因分類為不同的功能類別，以確定某些類別的分泌組基因在果實成熟期間是否主要受到轉錄和／或轉錄後調控。(Classify the genes into different functional categories to determine whether certain classes of secretome genes are primarily under transcriptional and/or post-transcriptional control during ripening.)

</&>

<h1>
 番茄果皮組織轉錄組之組織特異性分析：提高分泌組研究特異性的方法(Tissue specific analysis of the tomato pericarp tissues transcriptome: an approach to increase specificity in secretome studies.)
</h1>

<div class="indentedcontent">
  <p>
  大多數關於與果實膨大和成熟相關並控制果實膨大和成熟的生化與調控途徑的研究都是基於均質化的整體組織，並未考慮提取分析物（轉錄本、蛋白質或代謝物）的多種不同細胞類型。因此，潛在有價值的空間資訊會遺失，且僅在某些細胞類型中表現的較低豐度細胞組分可能會被稀釋至檢測限以下。(Most studies of the biochemical and regulatory pathways that are associated with, and control, fruit expansion and ripening are based on homogenized bulk tissues, and do not take into consideration the multiplicity of different cell types from which the analytes (transcripts, proteins or metabolites) are extracted. Consequently, potentially valuable spatial information is lost and the lower abundance cellular components that are expressed only in certain cell types can be diluted below the level of detection.)
  </p>

  <div style="width: 700px" class="captioned_image caption_right">

    <img src="/documents/img/secretom/tomato_pericarp_section_500.jpg" />

    <p style="margin-top: 2em; height: 100%">
    穿過番茄果實果皮的橫截面光學顯微鏡影像，包含數種組織類型：外表皮、厚角組織、薄壁組織、維管束組織和內表皮。(Light microscope image of a cross section through a tomato fruit pericarp, which comprises several tissue types: outer epidermis, collenchyma, parenchyma, vascular tissues, and inner epidermis.)
    </p>

  </div>

  <p>
  我們正在使用雷射捕捉顯微切割(LMD)，結合使用 RNAseq 進行轉錄分析，以識別組織類型特異性的轉錄本和分子途徑，從而對組織特異性基因表現乃至組織和器官生理學獲得新見解。在這方面，我們對界定組織特異性分泌組特別感興趣。此外，對轉錄組的深入挖掘對番茄基因註釋極具價值；例如揭示了大量可變剪接，這對於增強蛋白質體分析至關重要。(We are using laser capture microdissection (LMD), coupled with transcript profiling using RNAseq to identify tissue type specific transcripts and molecular pathways, in to gain new insights into aspects of tissue-specific gene expression, and consequently tissue and organ physiology. In this regard, we are particularly interested in defining tissue-specific secretomes. In addition, this deeper mining of the transcriptome is extremely valuable for tomato gene annotation; for example, revealing substantial alternative splicing, which in turn is critical for enhancing the proteome analyses.)
  </p>
</div>

<div class="indentedcontent">
  <div style="width: 240px; " class="captioned_image img_float_right">

    <img src="/documents/img/secretom/tomato_pericarp_section_LMD_x300.jpg" />

    <p>
    使用 LMD 去除維管束組織後的番茄果實果皮切片。(Tomato fruit pericarp section after removal of the vascular tissue using LMD.)
    </p>

  </div>

  <div style="float; left; width: 430px">
  <&| /secretom/section_templates/objectives.mas, is_subsection => 1 &>

    利用 454 和 Illumina 技術，在各個發育階段構建並測序番茄果實果皮中每種組織的特異性轉錄文庫(Construct and sequence tissue specific transcript libraries for each tissue in tomato fruit pericarp, using 454 and Illumina technologies , at various developmental stages)

    表徵各組織的預測分泌組(Characterize the predicted secretomes of each tissue)

    利用轉錄本的高深度覆蓋來改善基因空間定義，進而促進蛋白質體研究的胜肽匹配(Use the deep coverage of the transcripts to identify enhance gene space definition, and therefore peptide matching for the proteomic studies)

  </&>
  </div>

  <p>
  迄今為止，分佈在各組織文庫中總共產生了 1,456,024 條高質量序列。序列組裝後，20,976 個番茄單基因（由至少五個讀段組裝）與一個或多個組織相關聯。(To date, a total of 1,456,024 high quality sequences have been generated, distributed among the tissue libraries. Following sequence assembly, 20,976 tomato unigenes (assembled from at least five reads) were associated with one or more of the tissues.)
  </p>

</div>

